00:04:29.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Michael pulled out his cell phone and dialed the Porcos' home number twice, but nothing stirred within the house. Michael then called his boss, who encouraged him to go up and knock on the front door. Michael kept his boss on the line as he headed up the driveway, and immediately realized something was amiss. The front door was slightly ajar and a key had been left in the lock. Worse still, a large smear of blood was visible on the doorknob, and several droplets were splattered around the porch.
迈克尔掏出手机，拨打了两次波科家的座机号码，但屋里毫无动静。迈克尔随即打电话给他的老板，老板鼓励他走过去敲前门。迈克尔一边沿着车道走，一边让老板保持通话，并立即意识到情况有些不对劲。前门微微敞开着，钥匙还插在锁上。更糟糕的是，门把手上明显有一大片血迹，门廊周围还溅落了数滴血。

8
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:55.000
Michael could hear the Porcos' pet golden retriever barking from somewhere inside. He asked his boss whether he should go in and was told to enter with caution. Michael carefully peered into the foyer before informing his boss. This is a crime scene, call an ambulance. At the base of the stairs, Peter Porco was lying motionless on the tiled floor, his eyes open and glazed. Blood from a severe head injury had soaked his clothes and was smeared all around him, including along the walls and on some interior doors.
迈克尔听到波科家的宠物金毛寻犬在屋里的某个地方吠叫。他问老板自己是否应该进去，老板告诉他要小心进入。迈克尔小心翼翼地窥视着门厅，然后告诉老板：“这是一个犯罪现场，快叫救护车。”在楼梯底部，彼得·波科面朝下倒在瓷砖地板上一动不动，双眼睁开且毫无光泽。严重头部受伤流出的血浸透了他的衣服，并涂抹在他周围的各处，包括墙壁和一些内门上。

9
00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:36.000
Someone had walked through the blood, leaving red footprints throughout the crime scene. Paramedic Kevin Robert was driving his ambulance in a nearby street when he received a call notifying him of the situation unfolding on Broccoli Drive. He reached the Porco house and was summoned to the first floor by a detective who had arrived minutes earlier. Kevin carefully stepped around Peter Porco's lifeless body, ascended the stairs and entered the main bedroom. Inside, Joan Porco was lying horizontally across a blood-soaked bed.
有人曾踩着血走过，在整个犯罪现场留下了红色的脚印。急救人员凯文·罗伯特正驾驶着救护车在附近的一条街道上行驶，这时他接到一个电话，通知他布罗科利大道上正在发生紧急情况。他赶到波科家，被几分钟前到达的一名侦探叫上了二楼。凯文小心翼翼地绕过彼得·波科毫无生气的尸体，走上楼梯，进入了主卧室。在里面，琼·波科横躺在一张血迹斑斑的床铺上。

10
00:06:36.000 --> 00:07:27.000
The walls above her were splattered in blood, as were the bedside tables. Joan's upper arms and hands had lacerations indicative of defensive wounds, but it was her head that had bore the brunt of the attack. One of her eyes was split in half and the side of her jaw was hanging from her face. Joan had been struck three times to her face and head while she was sleeping. The direction of the cast-off indicated only one assailant had carried out the violent assault. Lying at the foot of the bed was an axe covered in blood. The assailant had unleashed the same axe on Peter Porco a total of 16 times.
她头顶上方的墙壁上溅满了血迹，床头柜也是如此。琼的上臂和手部有表明是防御性伤口的撕裂伤，但遭受袭击最严重的部位是她的头部。她的一只眼睛裂成两半，侧脸的下巴挂在脸上。琼在睡觉时面部和头部遭到了三次重击。挥洒血迹的方向表明，只有一名凶手实施了这起暴力袭击。床脚躺着一把沾满血迹的斧头。凶手对彼得·波科挥舞了同一把斧头足足16次。

11
00:07:27.000 --> 00:08:02.000
As this was 13 more hits than his wife, it appeared as though Peter was the intended victim. Judging by the amount of blood trailed throughout the house, it was initially thought that Peter had tried to run from his attacker, who chased him and hit him repeatedly until he collapsed. But the bloody footprints throughout the house only belonged to Peter. He wasn't being pursued by anyone. A medical examiner was able to shed light on the bizarre scenario that took place in
由于这比对他妻子的袭击多出13次，因此彼得似乎才是原本的目标。从全屋拖拽的血迹来看，最初人们认为彼得曾试图从袭击者手中逃跑，而凶手追赶他并反复击打他，直到他倒下。然而，房子里的血迹脚印只属于彼得。没有人尾随追赶他。法医得以揭开那天早上在屋里发生的诡异情景。

12
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:45.000
the house that morning. An autopsy showed that Peter had sustained severe damage to part of the brain responsible for higher-order functions such as perception, decision-making and language. However, the part of the brain that controls primal instinct and well-formed habits was undamaged. What actually happened was that like his wife, Peter was set upon while in bed. The killer had fled after carrying out the attack, unaware that Peter was still alive. Shortly after, Peter awoke to the sound of his alarm clock.
尸检显示，彼得的大脑中负责感知、决策和语言等高级功能的区域受到了严重损伤。然而，控制原始本能和熟练习惯的大脑区域却完好无损。实际情况是，彼得和他的妻子一样，是在床上遭到袭击的。凶手在行凶后逃离，并不知道彼得还活着。不久之后，彼得被闹钟的声音唤醒。

13
00:08:45.000 --> 00:09:31.000
The part of his brain that would otherwise perceive his injured state was too damaged to function properly. So even when he stared at his caved-in skull in the bathroom mirror and began cleaning up his own dripping blood, Peter was unable to comprehend that he was critically hurt and needed urgent medical attention. However, his brain was still functioning in some capacity, allowing him to carry out his morning routine on instinct alone until he succumbed to blood loss. This was not the first time that Detective Chris Boudish had attended the Porco House.
他大脑中原本能感知自己受伤状态的部分受损严重，无法正常运作。因此，甚至当他在浴室镜子里凝视自己凹陷的头骨并开始清理自己滴落的鲜血时，彼得也无法理解自己受了重伤，需要紧急医疗救助。然而，他的大脑仍在某种程度上运转，使他仅凭本能完成了早上的日常起居，直到他因失血过多而倒下。这并不是侦探克里斯·鲍迪什第一次来到波科家。

14
00:09:31.000 --> 00:10:12.000
Almost two years prior, he was called to the address following reports of a burglary. Peter and Joan had been awaiting the detective on their front porch. They were stressed, having just discovered that two laptops had been stolen from their house. The offender had seemingly gained access via the garage window by opening its frame and cutting through its mesh screen in a semi-circular manner. Lack of evidence prevented any arrests for the break-in, but it did prompt Peter and Joan to bolt the window shut and install a home security system.
将近两年前，他曾因接到入室盗窃的报告而被召至该地址。彼得和琼当时正在前廊等候侦探。他们感到压力很大，因为刚发现家里被偷了两台笔记本电脑。作案者似乎是通过车库窗户进入的，他撬开窗框，并以半圆形的方式割破了纱窗。由于缺乏证据，这起入室盗窃案未能逮捕任何人，但这确实促使彼得和琼把窗户用螺栓锁死，并安装了家庭安防系统。

15
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:56.000
In a town with a low crime rate, the burglary had stuck in Detective Boudish's mind and when Peter and Joan were found brutally attacked, he suspected a link between the two incidents. In both cases, the mesh screen of a window leading to the garage had been cut in a similar semi-circular manner. But during the murders, the intruder had also cut the home's phone line. They also smashed the LCD screen of the security system in the foyer. Only a single foreign fingerprint was found at the crime scene. It was uncovered on the door leading to the basement, where the couple's dog had been
在一个犯罪率很低的城镇里，这起入室盗窃案一直留在鲍迪什侦探的脑海里，当发现彼得和琼遭到残酷袭击时，他怀疑这两起事件之间存在联系。在这两起案件中，通往车库的窗户纱窗都以类似的半圆形方式被割破。但在谋杀案发生期间，入侵者还切断了家里的电话线。他们还砸碎了门厅安防系统的液晶屏幕。犯罪现场只发现了一个外国人的指纹。它是在通往地下室的门上被发现的，夫妻俩的狗就被关在那里。

16
